      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T18:12:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. Do you plan to refactor it? I think it\u0027s good to keep the paths relative, so that it can match both \u0027/\u003cp\u003e\u0027 and \u0027/system/\u003cp\u003e\u0027, as the comment suggests. Note that `system_ext` and `product` can be folders under `/system` instead of standalone partitions on some devices (e.g., https://android-build.corp.google.com/artifact/submitted/11997608/aosp_arm64-userdebug/latest/view/installed-files.txt). The pattern matching here has to handle this case.\n\nEven if you still think supporting leading `/`s is necessary, to avoid double `/`, you can simply use `filepath.Join(\u0027/\u0027, f)` instead of `f` on the next line.",
      "parentUuid": "e29c1a5e_e9ad1743",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 535,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 538,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "9cb0b14dbaf7cbcb3a8cef1161e3f2ed42ae5f1a",
