      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T18:41:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Keeping the paths relative in `SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX_FILTER` seems reasonable, and I do not have any upcoming plans to fix it. Could you point me to where this pattern matching is done? (I think soong might have a different implementation in `makeFileMatch`)\n\nBut I think we need to add a starting `/` here. Without it, the behavior might not be correct, as surfaced by this test\n```\n$ --- FAIL: TestDexPreoptSystemOther (0.00s)                                                                                                       \n    dexpreopt_test.go:176: \n        want installs:\n           out/soong/Ptest/oat/arm/package.odex:/system_other/product/app/test/oat/arm/Ptest.odex out/soong/Ptest/oat/arm/package.vdex:/system_other/product/app/test/oat/arm/Ptest.vdex\n        got:\n           out/soong/Ptest/oat/arm/package.odex:/product/app/test/oat/arm/Ptest.odex out/soong/Ptest/oat/arm/package.vdex:/product/app/test/oat/arm/Ptest.vdex        \nFAIL                                                                                                                                             \nFAIL    android/soong/dexpreopt 0.099s                                                                                                           \nFAIL\n```\n\nI think this happens because [makeFileMatch](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/1b072bfda5a46daf2f331b72d899a9939695db32:dexpreopt/dexpreopt.go;l\u003d566-568;drc\u003d5ae65ee6e060815dc5f3c11b505a313a3c37317c;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0) looks for the prefix rather than the substring. I have updated the implementation with `filepath.Join`\n\nFor the aosp_arm64 example, I think it is covered by `!global.HasSystemOther` in line 522?",
